-## Measured semantics — out of scope
+## Measured semantics
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per turn after the round loop exits and is passed the sum of every provider call's usage in that turn, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit receives the complete cost even for turns that ran multiple tool rounds. ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call in a turn that ran two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/usageAcrossRounds.acceptance.test.ts#L66))
+- `afterModelResponse` sums only the rounds that reported usage; rounds that reported none are skipped, so a turn where no round reports still delivers `undefined` to the hook. ([validated by: sums only the rounds that reported usage, skipping rounds that reported none](../../src/orchestration/usageAcrossRounds.acceptance.test.ts#L72), [validated by: reports nothing when no round reported usage](../../src/orchestration/usageAcrossRounds.acceptance.test.ts#L78))
+- The internal `accumulateUsage` helper sums two `UsageMetadata` values field by field when both are defined. ([validated by: sums two defined UsageMetadata values field by field](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L32))
+- `accumulateUsage` returns `undefined` when both operands are `undefined`. ([validated by: returns undefined when both operands are undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L36))
+- `accumulateUsage` returns the defined operand unchanged when the other is `undefined`. ([validated by: returns the defined second operand when first is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L40), [validated by: returns the defined first operand when second is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L44))
 
-- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+### Background
+
+These properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L151](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L151)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
